DATA SOURCES
================================================================================

Open Tree of Life — synthesis v16.1 (`opentree16.1`), taxonomy OTT 3.7.3
    CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication).
    Declared in the release's own `properties.json` as `"legal": "cc0"`.
    The dedication covers Open Tree's assembly; it does not relicense the
    upstream taxonomies Open Tree reconciles (NCBI, GBIF, WoRMS, IRMNG,
    Index Fungorum, SILVA).
    https://tree.opentreeoflife.org/

Duke, J. D., Guo, Y., Forest, F., Gumbs, R., McTavish, E. J. & Rosindell, J.
(2026). "Assembling a fully-dated complete tree of life."
    CC-BY 4.0. ATTRIBUTION REQUIRED.
    Data: Zenodo, doi:10.5281/zenodo.19049120
    Preprint: bioRxiv, doi:10.64898/2026.03.05.709771
    Supplies `age_ma`, `age_tier` and the phase-2 basis of `age_layout`.
    Interpolation code: github.com/jdduke24/dated-complete-tree (BSD-3-Clause).

International Commission on Stratigraphy — `chart.ttl`, version 2026/06
    CC-BY 4.0. ATTRIBUTION REQUIRED.
    Cite: Cohen, K. M., Finney, S. C., Gibbard, P. L. & Fan, J.-X.,
    "The ICS International Chronostratigraphic Chart", Episodes 2025;48:105-115.
    Supplies `build/timescale.json` — interval names, ages, ranks and the
    official CGMW colours.
    https://github.com/i-c-stratigraphy/chart

Wikidata
    CC0 1.0 Universal.
    Properties P9157 (Open Tree of Life ID), P225 (taxon name), P1843 (taxon
    common name), plus item labels and aliases. Supplies the `vernacular`
    table (162,466 rows) — the search box's entire common-name vocabulary.
    https://www.wikidata.org/

Paleobiology Database (PBDB)
    CC0 1.0 Universal, as declared by the data service on delivery.
    Supplies the `fossil` table (523,112 rows), first/last appearance
    brackets, the `occurrence` table, the fossil attachment points that
    rewrite `age_layout`, and the vernacular names in `VernacularName.tsv`.
    https://paleobiodb.org/

    The declaration is preserved verbatim in `snapshot/pbdb/datainfo.json`,
    which the API returns alongside the data itself:

        data_license: Creative Commons CC0
        license_url:  https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/
        access_time:  Sat 2026-08-01 01:08:29 GMT

    That block, with its access timestamp and re-runnable `data_url`, is also
    the citation PBDB asks for. Note for anyone auditing this: PBDB's classic
    site FAQ states CC BY-NC-ND 3.0 and GBIF's listing of the same checklist
    states CC BY 4.0. The CC0 declaration above is the one attached to the
    retrieval, is machine-readable and current, and CC0 is irrevocable once
    made — so it governs this data as retrieved on the date recorded.

GBIF — legacy backbone taxonomy (frozen 2023-08-28) and the PBDB checklist
Darwin Core archive (dataset c33ce2f2-c3cc-43a5-a380-fe4526d63650)
    Used only as an identifier bridge: PBDB `taxon_no` → GBIF `taxonID` →
    `nubKey` → OTT `gbif:` source id. No GBIF names, descriptions, taxonomic
    hierarchy or occurrence records are redistributed. The derived `xref`
    table (5,216,831 rows) is a correspondence between numeric identifiers
    and nothing else.
    https://www.gbif.org/

PhyloPic
    MIXED, PER IMAGE. See "Silhouettes" below.
    12,863 SVGs mirrored byte-for-byte under `snapshot/phylopic/`, each
    verified by SHA-256. No image is recoloured, cropped, retraced or
    otherwise modified; the application displays them unaltered.
    https://www.phylopic.org/

TimeTree
    EXCLUDED. TimeTree's terms prohibit redistribution of its data and of
    transformations of its data. No TimeTree-derived age appears anywhere in
    this project, and none may be added.


================================================================================
SILHOUETTES
================================================================================

Every silhouette carries its own licence, its original creator and its
uploader. These are stored per image in the `silhouette` table
(`license_url`, `attribution`, `contributor`) and rendered to the reader in
the node card alongside a link to the licence itself.

Creator and uploader are DIFFERENT FIELDS and differ for roughly half the
corpus. `attribution` is the artist; `contributor` is whoever uploaded the
work. Credit the artist. Any surface that adds a second credit block must go
through `normalise` in `web/src/api.ts`, which is the only place that knows
both vocabularies.

Distribution across the mirrored corpus:

    CC0 1.0                 6,661   51.8%
    CC-BY 4.0               2,432   18.9%   attribution required
    CC-BY-SA 3.0            1,196    9.3%   attribution required, ShareAlike
    CC-BY 3.0               1,059    8.2%   attribution required
    Public Domain Mark        770    6.0%
    CC-BY-NC 3.0              420    3.3%   NON-COMMERCIAL ONLY
    CC-BY-NC-SA 3.0           325    2.5%   NON-COMMERCIAL ONLY
                           ------
                           12,863

Two consequences worth stating plainly:

  * 745 images (5.8%) are NonCommercial. The build pipeline deliberately
    applies no NonCommercial filter — see `pipeline/src/concestor_build/
    images.py` and `docs/handoff.md` §1 — because the project is not
    commercial. ANY COMMERCIAL USE OF THIS DATASET MUST FILTER THEM OUT
    FIRST, and that includes advertising or sponsorship on an otherwise free
    hosted instance. The `license_url` column carries everything needed.

    Measured against build b48553b2b8a4a2ed, what filtering costs:

        357 NC images are actually in use
        128,719 nodes (4.7%) currently resolve to one
        88 of 885 divergence witnesses (9.9%), across 38 distinct taxa

    Coverage does not fall — `node_image` borrows the closest drawn relative,
    so every node keeps a picture. What rises is `clade_idx`: the affected
    nodes silently begin claiming more than they do today. Per
    `docs/handoff.md` §5 that number, not coverage, is the one to gate on.
    The best-known witnesses are unaffected — Acanthostega gunnari is BY-SA
    3.0, Pakicetus BY 3.0, Sahelanthropus tchadensis CC0.

  * 1,521 images (11.8%) are ShareAlike. Because they are displayed
    unmodified and are not combined into a new work, ShareAlike imposes no
    obligation on this repository's own code. Tracing, recolouring or
    otherwise adapting a ShareAlike silhouette would change that, and the
    resulting work would inherit BY-SA. See `docs/phase5c-decision.md` §9,
    which settles this for the deferred outline-generation phase.


